From 2faaf1fc4f0e73064c7ba28ab01bc19fafadf59c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 05:01:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: OPTIONS-REGISTRY POWERINFER_IOCP measured row
 (same-binary A/B)

Replace the placeholder cost cell with the clean isolation result. Same binary,
same HEAD, fresh server per arm, env flip only - this removes the HEAD confound
that made the first IOCP arm uninterpretable.

  OFF (POWERINFER_IOCP=0): 3.77 / 3.60 / 5.94 / 3.94  (mean 4.31)
  ON  (POWERINFER_IOCP=1): 2.42 / 8.74 / 5.20 / 6.28  (mean 5.66)

Direction: IOCP does NOT regress the read path. The earlier "flat, lean
regression" reading came from comparing a single IOCP arm against the historical
B-arm, which is a different HEAD and a different memory regime; that flag is
retired.

Magnitude stays UNMEASURED and the +31% is recorded as an UPPER BOUND, not an
estimate: one roll per cell, heavily overlapping ranges, both arms under memory
pressure (2.4-4.0 GB free during), and two confounds favour ON - it ran second
(warmer page cache) and launched with 1.2 GB more headroom.

Streaming confirmed engaged in BOTH arms (working set 4.77 GB vs an 11.4 GB
model file). Zero IOCP errors either arm. Ring-full (n_inflight >= 512) and
ERROR_IO_PENDING remain unexercised and are recorded as such.

Ported-mechanism: n/a - measurement record for an existing runtime option
Source-path: docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/run-journal.jsonl, m2b-ab-summary.log, m2b-ab-A-sync.log, m2b-ab-B-iocp.log
Origin: ArifiLabs/iocp-async
---
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
index 3a5b5451c..e20ead96c 100644
--- a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
+++ b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ safe measurement posture.
 |---|---|---|---|---|
 | `EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH` | unset | Loads a generated Q4_0 expert bundle from SSD for supported MoE models. | Use when the model’s experts cannot remain in RAM/VRAM and a compatible bundle exists. | Capability proven: 21B streamed coherently at `5.9–6.1` CPU decode t/s; Qwen3.6-35B streamed from a 17 GB bundle at `1.6` CPU decode t/s; tiered `-ngl 99 -cmoe` reached `3.0` t/s. It is not a claim of sparse Vulkan execution. |
 | `MAX_N_CACHED` | implementation-selected; document the chosen value in a run record | Bounds hot-expert RAM cache capacity. | Increase only after measuring cache pressure, RAM headroom, and bundle I/O behavior. | No independently accepted ON/OFF benchmark is recorded. Treat as a measured tuning variable, not a presumed gain. |
-| `POWERINFER_IOCP` | **ON** when unset (Windows only; any value other than an exact `0` keeps IOCP). `POWERINFER_IOCP=0` selects the pre-M2b synchronous path. | Scope: the Windows expert-bundle read path only (`powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp` + the `io_worker_main` Windows branch); it is inert on Linux, which keeps vendored `io_uring` unconditionally. ON issues bounded IOCP async positioned reads (ring of `io_queue_depth`=512) so storage latency overlaps the token path; OFF issues blocking `ReadFile`+`OVERLAPPED` positioned reads, one at a time. | Flip to `0` to recover from a suspected streaming deadlock, an IOCP assert, or to A/B the read path without a recompile. Only meaningful with `EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH` set — with no bundle there is no expert IO and the flag does nothing. | **Cost ON: UNMEASURED (indeterminate).** Single arm on this box (2026-07-24, llama-server 21B+bundle-21b, `-ngl 0 -b 8 -ub 8`, 4× n64 ignore_eos) gave `5.47 / 5.55 / 5.28 / 4.84` t/s — coherent, zero IOCP errors, but **no warm-cache climb** and flat-to-declining. Not attributable: free RAM was pinned `3.15–3.55 GB` (sustained sub-floor) and the binary carries ternary-g128 + phase-3a, so it is not a same-HEAD isolation. **Cost OFF: UNMEASURED on this HEAD.** Sol's audit *estimate* of a `10–40%` cold-regime gain is an estimate, never measured on this box (`RESULTS-sparse-runs-on-windows.md:286`; codex job `task-mrwgwtze-hw1o8t.log`) — do not cite it as a result. Correctness ON is proven: streaming engaged (working set `4.76 GB` vs an `11.4 GB` model file), coherent ×4, clean shutdown. Ring-full (`n_inflight ≥ 512`) and `ERROR_IO_PENDING` branches remain unexercised. |
+| `POWERINFER_IOCP` | **ON** when unset (Windows only; any value other than an exact `0` keeps IOCP). `POWERINFER_IOCP=0` selects the pre-M2b synchronous path. | Scope: the Windows expert-bundle read path only (`powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp` + the `io_worker_main` Windows branch); it is inert on Linux, which keeps vendored `io_uring` unconditionally. ON issues bounded IOCP async positioned reads (ring of `io_queue_depth`=512) so storage latency overlaps the token path; OFF issues blocking `ReadFile`+`OVERLAPPED` positioned reads, one at a time. | Flip to `0` to recover from a suspected streaming deadlock, an IOCP assert, or to A/B the read path without a recompile. Only meaningful with `EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH` set — with no bundle there is no expert IO and the flag does nothing. | **Direction known, magnitude UNMEASURED. IOCP does not regress the read path.** Same-binary A/B, 2026-07-24 (llama-server, 21B + bundle-21b, `-ngl 0 -b 8 -ub 8`, 4× n64 ignore_eos, fresh server per arm, env flip only — no HEAD confound): **OFF `3.77 / 3.60 / 5.94 / 3.94`** (mean `4.31`) vs **ON `2.42 / 8.74 / 5.20 / 6.28`** (mean `5.66`). Nominally `+31%` on the mean, but **do not quote that number**: single roll per cell, ranges overlap heavily, both arms ran under pressure (`2.4–4.0 GB` free during), and two confounds favour ON — it ran second (warmer page cache) and launched with `1.2 GB` more headroom. Treat `+31%` as an upper bound. Sol's `10–40%` cold-regime figure is an audit *estimate*, never measured here (`RESULTS-sparse-runs-on-windows.md:286`; codex job `task-mrwgwtze-hw1o8t.log`) — do not cite it as a result. Correctness ON is proven: streaming engaged (working set `4.77 GB` vs an `11.4 GB` model file, identical in both arms), coherent output, zero IOCP errors, clean shutdown. Ring-full (`n_inflight ≥ 512`) and `ERROR_IO_PENDING` branches remain **unexercised**. |
 | `LANE110_PROF=1` | unset | Emits per-operation timing for pipeline initialization, scheduling, build tasks, and forward execution. | Diagnosis only. Disable for benchmark runs. | Pipeline-init reuse itself reduced rebuild work from `2472 µs` to `0–2 µs`; profiler overhead has not been independently quantified. |
 | `LANE110_PREFETCH_CAP` | implementation default, currently `3*n_expert_used` | Limits standalone expert prefetch aggressiveness. | Sweep under cache pressure after establishing the baseline. | Recorded server sequences: default approximately `[5.07/9.03/9.58/12.01]`; cap `1` `[5.13/9.88/10.29/11.22]`; cap `96` `[5.79/11.73/12.19/11.26]`. Default retained because apparent ramp differences require controlled retest. |
 | `--ctx-checkpoints 0` | `0` | Disables server prompt rewind/checkpoints. | Keep off unless a workload demonstrably requires rewind semantics. | Largest historical gain: stock rewind `39.9/68.4/280`; ON_DEVICE checkpoint `84.8/128.8/341.6`; disabled approximately `101/150/372` across short/medium/long prefill. |
